 /* Admin shared styles — extracted verbatim from +page.svelte <style>.
- * Plain CSS import = global scope. Two deliberate transforms:
- * - `:global(body)` → `body` (was already global).
- * - `.controls :global(x)` → `.dashboard .controls x`: the piercing
- *   rules target panel-child internals; the prefix keeps admin-only
- *   scope and pre-extraction specificity. No app.css collisions.
+ *
+ * A plain CSS import is GLOBAL, and the app is client-routed, so once /admin
+ * has been visited these rules stay loaded on every later route. Bare
+ * `.stat`, `.btn`, `label`, `select`… were reaching /admin/fleet/health and
+ * the kiosk's TelemetryPanel. Every rule is therefore scoped under the page
+ * root:
+ * - `:where(.dashboard) x` — `:where()` adds ZERO specificity, so the cascade
+ *   inside the admin page is unchanged (a `.dashboard x` prefix would have
+ *   out-ranked the panel components' own scoped rules).
+ * - `body` → `body:has(.dashboard)` — applies only while the admin root is
+ *   mounted (app.css sets no body rule; `:has()` needs Chromium ≥ 105).
+ * - `.controls :global(x)` → `.dashboard .controls x`: the piercing rules
+ *   target panel-child internals; the prefix keeps pre-extraction specificity.
  */
-	body {
+	body:has(.dashboard) {
 		margin: 0;
 		background: var(--bg-base);
 		color: var(--text);
